   "source": [
    "# Phase 2 — Historical Hazard Timeline\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project:** *How Often Would a Satellite Have Warned You?* — retrospective satellite\n",
    "space-time coincidence analysis for hazardous sea states along the **Lisbon → Halifax**\n",
    "North Atlantic shipping corridor (base paper: Kytariolou & Themelis, 2022, *J. Navigation* 75(6)).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Walk the CMEMS global wave reanalysis (3-hourly, 0.2°) along the route,\n",
    "flag every route-waypoint × time-step whose sea state is hazardous, and write a\n",
    "per-year **hazard catalogue** consumed by `phase3_coincidence.ipynb`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Output (one file per year):** `data/hazard_catalogue_{year}.parquet` — one row per flagged event.\n",
    "\n",
    "| column | type | meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `event_id` | str | `\"{year}_{i:05d}\"` |\n",
    "| `datetime` | Timestamp, tz=UTC | event time |\n",
    "| `lon`, `lat` | float | event position [°E, °N] |\n",
    "| `Hs_cmems` | float | significant wave height, CMEMS reanalysis [m] |\n",
    "| `T0_cmems` | float | peak wave period [s] |\n",
    "| `U10_era5` | float | 10-m wind speed, ERA5 [m/s] (NaN where ERA5 is not available) |\n",
    "| `flag_heave` | bool | `Hs > HEAVE_THRESH_M` |\n",
    "| `flag_rogue` | bool | `Hs > ROGUE_HS_PROXY` |\n",
    "| `flag_any` | bool | `flag_heave OR flag_rogue` |\n",
    "| `route_seg_idx` | int | index into `ROUTE_LONS` / `ROUTE_LATS` |\n",
    "| `lon_bin` | str | 5° longitude bin, e.g. `\"-10_-5\"` |\n",
    "\n",
    "This schema is a **contract** with Phase 3 — column names must not change.\n",
    "One extra trailing column, `flag_reason`, is appended for backward compatibility with the\n",
    "Phase 3 notebook (it prints `flag_reason.value_counts()`).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cell 1 CONFIG controls which years are processed** (`YEAR_START`, `YEAR_END`).\n",
    "Each year is processed independently: a missing file or failed download skips that year only.\n",
    "\n",
    "All paths are relative to the project folder (the folder containing this notebook)."
   ]
  },
