    "## 2.5 Apply Hazard Flag\n",
    "\n",
    "Two complementary Hs-based criteria (the full Phase 1 seakeeping flag needs heave/roll RAOs):\n",
    "\n",
    "* `flag_heave` — `Hs > HEAVE_THRESH_M` (3.5 m), proxy for the significant-heave threshold of\n",
    "  the base paper (Sec. 4.6, `ship_physics.HEAVE_THRESHOLD_SIG_M`).\n",
    "* `flag_rogue` — `Hs > ROGUE_HS_PROXY` (6 m), grid-scale proxy for rogue-wave likelihood; it stands\n",
    "  in for $H_{max}/H_s > 2$ because individual-wave heights are not resolved by the reanalysis\n",
    "  (**limitation**).\n",
    "* `flag_any` — either flag."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "bed75347",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Section 2.5: hazard flags\n",
    "def apply_hazard_flags(df, heave_thresh, rogue_hs_proxy):\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    flag_heave : Hs > heave_thresh   (significant wave height proxy for the\n",
    "                 seakeeping threshold in [1] Sec 4.6)\n",
    "    flag_rogue : Hs > rogue_hs_proxy (grid-scale rogue-wave proxy; replaces\n",
    "                 H_max/Hs > 2 when individual-wave data is unavailable)\n",
    "    flag_any   : either flag is True\n",
    "\n",
    "    Note: the full flag ship_physics.is_hazardous_event() requires heave and\n",
    "    roll RAOs computed in Phase 1. Plug it in here once seakeeping_rao.py is\n",
    "    ready by replacing flag_heave with the Phase 1 output per waypoint.\n",
    "    NaN Hs never raises a flag.\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    df = df.copy()\n",
    "    df[\"flag_heave\"] = (df[\"Hs\"] > heave_thresh).astype(bool)\n",
    "    df[\"flag_rogue\"] = (df[\"Hs\"] > rogue_hs_proxy).astype(bool)\n",
    "    df[\"flag_any\"]   = df[\"flag_heave\"] | df[\"flag_rogue\"]\n",
    "    return df"
   ]
  },
