   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "- The table above gives, per year, the number of catalogued events, heave/rogue flag counts,\n",
    "  the maximum Hs and the share of events with ERA5 wind.\n",
    "- **Two-flag approach.** `flag_heave` (Hs > 3.5 m) and `flag_rogue` (Hs > 6 m) are Hs-only proxies\n",
    "  for the Phase 1 seakeeping flag. They are conservative: the real criterion is on *ship response*\n",
    "  (significant heave > 3.5 m, roll > 5°, H_max/H_s > 2), and a ship's significant heave is in general\n",
    "  smaller than the sea-surface Hs, so thresholding Hs flags more situations than the RAO-based\n",
    "  criterion would — it over-counts rather than misses hazards.\n",
    "- One row = one flagged route-waypoint × 3-hour step. A long storm therefore contributes several\n",
    "  correlated rows; decluster (merge consecutive steps per waypoint) before treating rows as independent events.\n",
    "- `data/hazard_catalogue_{year}.parquet` follows the Phase 3 contract (plus a trailing `flag_reason`\n",
    "  column) and is ready for `phase3_coincidence.ipynb` — set its `YEAR_START`/`YEAR_END` to the same years.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Limitations and Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "- Extend `YEAR_START`/`YEAR_END` beyond 2010–2020 (e.g. to 2024) once these years validate end-to-end with Phase 3.\n",
    "- Replace `flag_heave` / `flag_rogue` with `ship_physics.is_hazardous_event()` once\n",
    "  `seakeeping_rao.py` (Phase 1 step 1.2d) is complete.\n",
    "- Complete the ERA5 download (CDS API) for every month of the study period; until then `U10_era5` is NaN\n",
    "  where ERA5 is missing.\n",
    "- Consider an ensemble of routes (not just the straight-line route) as described in the project proposal\n",
    "  Phase 2 methodology."
   ]
